# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a change to the pipeline wiring.
#
# Copy this to .github/CODEOWNERS in your Salesforce repo and replace the owner
# with real GitHub users or a team (@org/team) — ideally two or more people,
# because GitHub never counts a PR author's own approval. GitHub ignores a line
# whose owner it does not know, so check the file on GitHub for errors after
# you push it.
#
# setup-branch-protection.sh turns on "Require review from Code Owners" for the
# entry and production branches (REQUIRE_CODE_OWNER_REVIEWS, on by default with
# REQUIRED_REVIEWS >= 1), so a PR touching a path below cannot merge until one
# of these owners approves it.
#
# Why these paths: the caller workflows decide what runs with your org
# credentials, and pipeline.config.yml decides every gate, test level and
# environment. A change to either changes how every deploy runs.
#
# The last matching line wins, so add any broader rules ABOVE these.

/.github/                         @your-org/pipeline-owners
/sf-pipeline/pipeline.config.yml  @your-org/pipeline-owners
